st14-zlayer-sky = sky

st14-trench-dug = You finish digging.
st14-trench-nothing-below = There is nothing below to dig into.
st14-trench-already-dug = This ground is already dug out.
st14-trench-mode = Spade: { $mode }.
st14-trench-mode-examine = Mode: [color=yellow]{ $mode }[/color]. Use it in hand to open the trench build window.
st14-trench-mode-name-trench = trench
st14-trench-mode-name-dugout = bunker
st14-trench-mode-name-steps = steps
st14-trench-mode-name-cable = cable trench
st14-trench-bad-spot = You can't dig here.
st14-trench-progress = { $percent }% dug
st14-trench-not-dug = There is no trench here yet.
st14-trench-steps-cut = You cut steps.
st14-trench-steps-filled = You fill the steps in.
st14-trench-steps-nowhere = Steps here would lead nowhere.
st14-trench-climb-blocked = You can't climb out here.
st14-trench-too-far = Too far away.
st14-trench-laid-out = Laid out. Walk up to it and dig.
st14-trench-menu-title = Earthworks
st14-trench-menu-hint = R to turn, click with the spade to lay out and dig. Close the window to put the ghost away.
st14-trench-menu-trench-desc = A trench: length 1-5 and width 1-2 tiles are set at the bottom of the window, the bigger the longer it takes to dig. No roof, you fire from it.
st14-trench-menu-dugout-desc = A 3x3 roofed bunker, closed all round. Bunkers built on to each other make one bunker structure. Doors go in the middles of the sides, cut with the spade.
st14-trench-menu-steps-desc = Steps on a trench tile. R picks where they lead. Again to fill them in.
st14-trench-menu-cable-desc = A small trench in the sand for an energy fence cable.
st14-climb-out-of-trench = Climb out of the trench
st14-climb-onto-bunker = Climb onto the roof
st14-climb-onto-dugout = Climb onto the bunker
st14-trench-mode-name-door = bunker door
st14-trench-menu-door-desc = Cut a door into a bunker: the middle of the side nearest the cursor. You choose which of the four.
st14-trench-no-dugout = There is no bunker here: a door is cut in the middle of its side.
st14-trench-door-open = There is a way through here already.
st14-trench-door-cut = You cut a door through the partition.
st14-trench-mode-name-fill = fill in
st14-trench-menu-fill-desc = Fill a trench tile back in: the ground comes back as round it, whoever is inside ends up on top. A bunker is not filled in this way.
st14-trench-filled = You fill the trench in.
st14-trench-fill-roofed = A bunker cannot be filled in.
st14-bunker-ramp-down = Go down the ramp
st14-bunker-ramp-up = Go up the ramp
st14-bunker-ladder-up = Climb onto the roof
st14-bunker-ladder-down = Climb down into the bunker
st14-bunker-passage-go = Go through
st14-construction-condition-dugout = Goes on a bunker (point at it from inside or from its roof), one upgrade a bunker.
st14-construction-condition-bunker-base = On a bunker in a bunker structure of 6 or more, no upgraded bunker next to it, no nearer than 20 tiles to another base.
st14-construction-condition-dugout-slit = Goes into the side of a bunker, in the middle of it.
st14-construction-condition-dugout-apart = Goes on a bunker with no upgraded bunker next to it.
st14-construction-condition-dugout-ramp = Goes on a bunker; R picks the side of the ramp, with flat ground past it.
st14-construction-condition-dugout-ladder = Goes inside a bunker, not in the middle.
st14-construction-condition-trench-mod = Goes on a trench tile, one modification a tile. R turns it.
st14-trench-mode-name-corner = corner bunker
st14-trench-menu-corner-desc = A corner bunker: half of a 3x3 square along its diagonal, a staircase of 6 tiles, roofed. It joins bunkers at a corner. R picks the corner of the right angle. It carries no upgrades; doors only on its whole sides.
st14-trench-menu-length = Trench length:
st14-trench-menu-width = Width:
